    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0604" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-24T15:00:00+08:00">May 24, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 24—10:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of May 22, 10 a.m.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d449-f1"/>
                    Canton Government again notified me yesterday that the offensive against Wuchow
                    is to be resumed with vigor both by land and water. I passed this information on
                    to commander of the South China Patrol who now informs me that the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Guam</hi> left Wuchow this morning with six Americans
                    for Hong Kong. This indicates that about thirty Americans have remained in
                    Wuchow in spite of warnings. Commander of the <hi rendition="#italic">Guam</hi>
                    reports that Kwangsi authorities will not defend Wuchow but intend to withdraw
                    to the interior.</p>
                <p>Private messengers from Shiuchow on Canton-Hankow Railway report that Communists
                    under Chu Teh are approaching the city which is defenseless. These Communists
                    have already looted several towns on northern border of Kwangsi and were
                    formerly active in southern Kwangsi. Consuls interested urged Cantonese
                    Government to send troops to protect Shiuchow, and the Government has promised
                    to despatch 1,000 men.</p>
                <p>The Legation has been informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
